  "text_pages": [
    "경희대학교\n바로가기 메뉴\n주메뉴 바로가기\n본문가기\nKHU Home\n발전기금\n인포21\nWebmail\n검색창 열기\n검색어\n검색\n검색창 닫기\nkor\n한국어\nAbout Us\nGreetings\nKHU at a Glance\nLocation\nContact Us\nPartnerships\nAnnouncement\nNotice\nOutgoing Program\nIncoming  Program\nPartner University Program\nCalendar\nIncoming\nExchange/Visiting\nGlobal Virtual School\nShort-term Program\nNews\nNews\nVideos\nOutgoing\nShort-term Program\nExchange Program\nInstitutional TOEFL\nFAQs\n영문홈페이지\n검색하기\n검색\n검색\n메뉴\nExchange/Visiting\n메인으로 이동\nIncoming\nAbout Us\nAnnouncement\nIncoming\nNews\nOutgoing\nExchange/Visiting\nExchange/Visiting\nGlobal Virtual School\nShort-term Program\nProgram Overview\nHOME\nExchange/Visiting\nProgram Overview\nProgram Overview\nInformation Sheet\nCourse Information\nCultural Program\n서브 컨텐츠\nExchange Student Program\nInternational students can take courses at Kyung Hee University either in Korean or English as an exchange student for up to one academic year.\nInternational students from partner institutions are eligible for our exchange program and their tuition at KHU is waived under the bilateral agreements.\nKHU currently offers over 30% of courses in English in a variety of fields including Management, Hotel and Tourism Management.\nVisiting Student Program\nVisiting Student Program allows you to spend 1-2 semesters at Kyung Hee University.\nWe eagerly provide you one of the best international study options in Korea.\nEligibility\nAcademic Requirements\n- Must be an currently enrolled undergraduate student at a four-year university\n- Must have an overall GPA of 2.5 out of 4.0 or above\n- Must have more than one semester remaining at home university after the completion of visiting program\nLanguage Proficiency\n- TOPIK Level 3 or above (Level 4 for College of Business Administration) - in case of taking courses conducted in Korean\n** Required minimum will be raised to TOPIK Level 5 or above, starting from Fall 2025**\n- TOEFL iBT 82 / IELTS 6.5 or higher recommended- in case of taking courses conducted in English\n* If applying to study in his/her native language, a proof of language proficiency is not required\nTuition and Fee\nStudents are responsible for tuition and living expenses in Korea\nTuition Fee: KRW 6,536,000 / Semester (Subject to change and may vary depending on the program)\nProcedure\n1. Apply to the exchange student program at your university's International Office : We require email  nomination from your university.\n* For Visiting Students Program :\nPlease email us to express your interest in participating in the visiting student program\nby (Spring semester) October 20 / (Fall semester) April 20\n.\nWe require a confirmation email from your home university that you are eligible to participate in the visiting program and transfer your credits back to your home university.\n2. Submit all Required documents to Kyung Hee University via online (Some may require post mail submission)\n- Complete list of documents required will be announced later to participating students\n3. Visa Issuance\n4. Book Flight Ticket\n5. Course Registration\n6. Dormitory Check-in\n7. Study at KHU with 2 exams(Midterm/Final)\n8. Receive transcript of record\nTHE ABOVE\nIS SUBJECT TO CHANGE"
  ],
